            <ArticleTitle>Urogenital/pelvic pain in men.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>213-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/SPC.0b013e3283523f19</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE OF REVIEW" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">The review is based on a Medline literature search using key words relating to male urogenital/pelvic pain for the years 2009-2011.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RECENT FINDINGS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The review covers those studies relating to cause, ongoing mechanisms and treatments.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SUMMARY" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The review highlights that the patients are often polysymptomatic with multimodal/system issues that require a team approach that involves multiple specialties and multiple disciplines.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
